{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Puts a wall clock over the engine’s turn counter, so a game can be played"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against an evening rather than a move count."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An adventure counts moves. A mystery counts minutes: every alibi in the house"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is stated as a time, and a player who cannot check one against a clock is being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked to take the game’s word for it. This library gives the move counter an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hour and a minute, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" verb that reads it back, alarms that go off at a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stated hour, and timetables that keep an actor where his day says he is.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"derived, not ticked"}]},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","isActive":true},{"text":" is a pure function of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engine’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so every rule, action, fuse and daemon in one turn reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time, the timer tick that closes the turn included. A clock advanced by a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"daemon of its own would be read differently by daemons sorting before and after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, which would make the hour depend on other timers’ names. Deriving also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inherits the engine’s own notion of world time: the hour doesn’t move on a parse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error or a meta command, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take all"},{"type":"text","text":" costs one turn rather than four."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle rather than a "},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"state to keep — the minutes a game has moved the clock by hand, whether it is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paused, and which stop each scheduled actor was last seen keeping. A bundle’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"globals namespace themselves and travel in save files, so the host lists the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clock in ","type":"text"},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and gets all three for nothing. Everything else belongs to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the host: the rooms, the actors, the bodies of the alarms, and the timetables. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" holds no state of its own, which is what lets a game declare one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as an ordinary computed property naming its own rooms, and what makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable\/location(at:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" an answer available at bootstrap, in a rule, and in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a plain unit test.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoClock          \/\/ .product(name: \"GnustoClock\", package: \"Gnusto\")","","struct Fulminate: Game {","    let clock = Clock(","        startingAt: TimeOfDay(17, 30),","        minutesPerTurn: 2,","        timeIs: { \"Your watch says \\($0).\" }","    )","","    var content: GameContents { clock }        \/\/ the verb, the action, the saved state","","    var timers: [TimedEvent] {","        clock.schedule(teague, daemonName: \"teague.day\", teagueDay)","","        clock.at(TimeOfDay(17, 46), named: \"clock.blast\") {","            blastHappened = true","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading the time needs a live turn, so "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now"},{"type":"text","text":" belongs in a rule body, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"describe","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block, an action or a timer, and not in a "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluated at bootstrap. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block that wants to place a scheduled actor asks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the timetable instead, which reads no world state:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"teague.starts(in: teagueDay.location(at: clock.start))"},{"type":"text","text":". A stored clock also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands the play-test status footer a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time=5:46 pm"},{"type":"text","text":" field, which a timed game"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wants, since a line true at half past five and false at six reads the same in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript that never says which it was."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoclock"]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"The clock","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock"],"anchor":"The-clock"},{"title":"Times of day","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeFormat"],"anchor":"Times-of-day"},{"title":"An actor’s day","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Stop"],"anchor":"An-actors-day"},{"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Gnusto"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"GnustoClock","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"GnustoClock"}],"title":"GnustoClock"},"references":{"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Gnusto":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Gnusto"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/TimeFormat":{"abstract":[{"text":"How a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","type":"reference"},{"text":" is spelled for the player.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeFormat"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"TimeFormat","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeFormat"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timeformat","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeFormat"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Timetable":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","title":"Timetable","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timetable","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Timetable","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An actor’s day, written down: a list of stops the clock walks them through."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timetable"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Timetable/location(at:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the actor is — or was, or will be — at a given time."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable\/location(at:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timetable\/location(at:)","title":"location(at:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"location"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"at"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","text":"TimeOfDay"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","text":"Location"}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock/now":{"title":"now","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What time it is now."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/now","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimeOfDay","preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV"}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock","title":"GnustoClock","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Puts a wall clock over the engine’s turn counter, so a game can be played"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against an evening rather than a move count."}],"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Stop":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Stop","title":"Stop","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Stop","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Stop","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"One appointment on an actor’s day: where they are meant to be, from when.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/stop"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock","title":"Clock","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Clock","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A wall clock over the turn counter: a game where it is twenty to six, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ten to six four turns later.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/TimeOfDay":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeOfDay","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"TimeOfDay","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeOfDay","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timeofday","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A time on a 24-hour wall clock, with no date attached: 8:15 in the evening"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeOfDay(20, 15)"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is the same value tomorrow."}]}}}